----- Test 6 -+- dir: . -+- cat macbeth.txt -----
    When shall we three meet again
    In thunder, lightning, or in rain?
        When the hurlyburly's done,
        When the battle's lost and won.
            That will be ere the set of sun.
    Where the place?
        Upon the heath.
            There to meet with Macbeth.
    I come, Graymalkin!
        Paddock calls.
            Anon.
                Fair is foul, and foul is fair:
                Hover through the fog and filthy air.

----- Test 7 -+- dir: . -+- cat sed.script -----
1,$ s/When/WHEN/g
1,$ s/and/\&/g
1,$ s/foul/nasty/g
1,$ s/is/==/g
1,$ s/meet/reunite/
1,$ s/of/de/
1,$ s/the/t'/g

----- Test 8 -+- dir: . -+- runsed macbeth.txt -----

----- Test 9 -+- dir: . -+- .runsed.diff.runsed -----
+ /usr/bin/diff ./.macbeth.txt.runsed macbeth.txt
1c1
<     When shall we three meet again
---
>     WHEN shall we three reunite again
3,8c3,8
<         When the hurlyburly's done,
<         When the battle's lost and won.
<             That will be ere the set of sun.
<     Where the place?
<         Upon the heath.
<             There to meet with Macbeth.
---
>         WHEN t' hurlyburly's done,
>         WHEN t' battle's lost & won.
>             That will be ere t' set de sun.
>     Where t' place?
>         Upon t' heath.
>             There to reunite with Macbeth.
12,13c12,13
<                 Fair is foul, and foul is fair:
<                 Hover through the fog and filthy air.
---
>                 Fair == nasty, & nasty == fair:
>                 Hover through t' fog & filthy air.


